      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have just found a workaround for this. Create assembly definition and check \"Override References\" , then never adding VRCCore-Editor to its \"Assembly References\".\nThis means the assembly never references VRCCore-Editor.\nIn this way, ConcurrentQueue<T> become accessible from the assembly.\nBut this also causes any classes in VRCCore-Editor become inaccessible from the assembly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-25T14:52:04.631Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue<T> is defined in both Unity's .NET4.X equivalent runtime and VRCCore-Editor.\nThis resulted in the type is inaccessible from non-precompiled script.\nSystem.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentQueue<T> doesn't exist in Unity's .NET3.5 equivalent runtime.\nBut latest version of VRCSDK2 or VRCSDK3 doesn't support .NET3.5 equivalent runtime, so we no longer need to define ConcurrentQueue<T> in VRCCore-Editor.\nPlease remove it from VRCCore-Editor.",
